<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>College Move-In: The Rental That Hauls the Dorm Room in One Trip</h1>
<p>Mini-fridge, futon, six totes, one nervous freshman. Here's the vehicle &mdash; and the mileage tier &mdash; that gets it all to campus without a second trip.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>Every August the same scene plays out in driveways across Jackson County: a sedan with its trunk open, a pile of dorm gear that clearly isn't going to fit, and a parent doing the mental math on a second 120-mile round trip.</p>
<p>Move-in season across western Wisconsin lands in <strong>late August and the first week of September</strong>, and the fix for the driveway math problem is simple: rent the right vehicle for one day and do it in one trip.</p>
<h2>The move-in workhorse: the 7-passenger minivan</h2>
<p>Our <a href="7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> ($78/day + $0.10/mile) is the vehicle we hand over most often for move-in runs. Fold the third row, tumble the second, and you've got a cargo bay that takes a mini-fridge, a futon, a desk chair, the tote-bin tower, and the student &mdash; with the sliding doors making the twentieth armload easier than the first.</p>
<p>A typical dorm load that would take a sedan three trips fits in a minivan once. That's the whole pitch.</p>
<h2>Lighter load? The SUV or a full-size car</h2>
<p>Second-year students moving into a furnished apartment, or anyone whose "dorm room" is really four totes and a laptop, can size down. The <a href="ford-edge-suv-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">Ford Edge SUV</a> (from $80/day) offers a tall, open cargo bay with the rear seats folded, and a full-size car ($65/day) handles a light load with the seats down.</p>
<h2>Pick the mileage tier before you go</h2>
<p>The campus runs from Black River Falls are predictable:</p>
<div style="background:#f8f9fb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:24px;margin-bottom:32px;">
<ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;">
<li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><strong>UW-Eau Claire:</strong> ~1 hour &middot; roughly 110 miles round trip</li>
<li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><strong>UW-La Crosse / Viterbo:</strong> ~1 hour &middot; roughly 110 miles round trip</li>
<li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><strong>UW-Stout (Menomonie):</strong> ~90 minutes &middot; roughly 170 miles round trip</li>
<li style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"><strong>Winona State:</strong> ~90 minutes &middot; roughly 140 miles round trip</li>
<li style="padding:10px 0;"><strong>UW-Madison:</strong> ~2 hours &middot; roughly 250 miles round trip</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p><strong>For cars and SUVs:</strong> every run on that list except a short local errand blows past the 100-mile daily cap on the local tier, so take the unlimited daily rate ($75 intermediate / $85 full-size / $100 SUV) and don't think about the odometer again.</p>
<p><strong>For the minivan:</strong> daily rentals are $0.10/mile from mile one, so the mileage is just arithmetic &mdash; an Eau Claire round trip adds about $11, Madison about $25. Even the Madison run totals right around $103 for the day. One trip, done.</p>
<h2>Book before the calendar collides</h2>
<p>Move-in weekends stack on top of end-of-summer vacations, and the minivans are the most popular vehicle in the fleet for both. Two to three weeks of lead time is the comfortable window &mdash; if move-in day is the last weekend of August, that means calling in mid-August at the latest.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> with your date and campus. Pickup is quick &mdash; if it's your first rental, our <a href="what-you-need-to-rent-a-car-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">first-timer's guide</a> covers the three documents to bring.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What's the best rental for college move-in?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The 7-passenger minivan &mdash; a full dorm room fits in one trip. Lighter loads fit the Ford Edge SUV or a full-size car.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Which mileage tier for a move-in day trip?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Cars and SUVs: unlimited daily &mdash; campus runs exceed the 100-mile local cap. Minivan: daily rate plus mileage; even Madison adds only ~$25.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Which campuses are within a day trip?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Eau Claire and La Crosse (~1 hr), Stout and Winona State (~90 min), Madison (~2 hrs) &mdash; all comfortable one-day moves.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">When should I book for move-in weekend?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Two to three weeks ahead. Move-in collides with end-of-summer trips and the minivans go first.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:48px;padding-top:32px;border-top:1px solid var(--light-gray);">
